MECHANISM: even AP {0,2,...,18} (high coverage via dilated lattice) + 2 odd bridges.
The 2 odd bridges keep gcd=1 robust to ANY single removal (the other odd survives),
so the config is genuine-wide; yet p0 is pushed above the decorrelated single-far floor Q.

VERDICT: kps HYP-2788's genuine-wide slack floor p0 < Q(k-1) is FALSE at k=12.
  k=10, k=11: slack floor HOLDS (exhaustive over span<=18: 0 over-Q; max p0 0.4295, 0.5118 < Q;
              random span<=30 even-dominant hunt: still 0 over-Q).
  k=12: slack floor BREAKS. EXACTLY 4 over-Q genuine-wide configs (exhaustive span<=18),
        all even-AP {0,2,..,18} + 2-odd-bridge; span 19..40 random hunt finds NO more.
  CRUCIAL: all breakers have p0 < cap (margin >= 0.24), so the LRC cap is NOT violated; only
  the INTERMEDIATE 'genuine-wide => p0<Q' reduction fails. The wide proof must bound p0<cap
  DIRECTLY for these shapes, not via the Q(k-1) slack floor.
